cdot \\mathbf{q}_i}.$ \n\nComputing $x_2,$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{2}}{{q}_{2}\\cdot {q}_{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4\\cdot 1+6\\cdot 1+(-2)\\cdot (-4)}{{1}^{2}+{1}^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{4+6+8}{1+1+16} \\\\  & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139535616 true] [17592186157014 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/5a56202f818d8b8d10dd06d5e4bd02ee0aabc2f16758ca64cb6dc416fb71075c.png) of $\\mathbb R^2,$ find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/d97e5bc94afc05532528354b82231eab87ca49ec72bd42879759c64c4165837d.png)" 13194139535616 true] [17592186157014 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $\\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix}$ of $\\mathbb R^2$, find $[\\mathbf{x}]_{\\mathcal{B}}$ if $\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535616 false] [17592186157014 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2$.\n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $\\begin{bmatrix}x_{1} \\\\ x_{2}\\end{bmatrix}$ where\n\n$$\nx_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i\n$$\n\nComputing the components of $\\mathbf{x}$, we get the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx_{1} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} =-2 - 6 =-8 \\\\\nx_{2} &= \\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{bmatrix} \\cdot \\begin{bmatrix}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{bmatrix} =-4 + 3 =-1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have $\\begin{bmatrix}-8 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535616 false] [17592186157014 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $\\mathcal{B}$ as $\\mathbf{q}_1,\\, \\mathbf{q}_2.$ \n\nSince $\\mathcal{B}$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/1ba0b151abea3c5b1a050c6ff924f3718fcb045b063b1b47df7a73f9d15316c9.png) where $x_i = \\mathbf{x} \\cdot \\mathbf{q}_i.$ Computing the components of $\\mathbf{x},$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ -\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-2-6=-8 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}-2\\sqrt{5} \\\\ 3\\sqrt{5}\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{5}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{5}}\\end{aligned}]=-4+3=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have ![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14066805/assets/51184680e9ec8b56a437334ca2a9281b1b364da2c35922839be13e545d92cec4.png)" 13194139535616 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357662 13194139535616 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357669 13194139535616 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357683 13194139535616 true] [17592186157210 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357690 13194139535616 true] [17592186157211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357648 13194139535616 true] [17592186157211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357655 13194139535616 true] [17592186157211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357676 13194139535616 true] [17592186157211 1020 #edb/ref 17592186357697 13194139535616 true] [17592186157710 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535616 true] [17592186157710 1100 "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of $R^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26x_{1}$, where $x_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}$.\n\n$B = {\\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ 2\\end{bmatrix}, \\begin{bmatrix}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{bmatrix}}, x = \\begin{bmatrix}3 \\\\ -1\\end{bmatrix}$" 13194139535616 false] [17592186157710 1100 "Given the orthogonal basis $B$ of ${R}^{2}$ and the vector $x$ below, find the value of $26{x}_{1},$ where ${x}_{1}$ is the first component of $[x]_{B}.$\n\n$$\nB={[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}-18 \\\\ 27\\end{aligned}]},\\,x=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]\n$$" 13194139535616 true] [17592186157710 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthogonal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{i}}{{q}_{i}\\cdot {q}_{i}}.$ Computing ${x}_{1},$ we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =\\frac{x\\cdot {q}_{1}}{{q}_{1}\\cdot {q}_{1}} \\\\  & =\\frac{3\\cdot 3+(-1)\\cdot 2}{{3}^{2}+{2}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{9-2}{9+4} \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{13}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n26{x}_{1}=26\\cdot \\frac{7}{13}=14.\n$$" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1017 #edb/ref 17592186357649 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1089 "q-102322" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1100 "Given the **orthonormal** basis $B={[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}],[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]}$ of ${R}^{2},$ find $[x]_{B}$ if $x=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].$" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1113 #uuid "ecfc4989-ba47-5e5d-ab5f-597b5de37da2" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357648 1145 "Let's denote the vectors of $B$ as ${q}_{1},\\,{q}_{2}.$ \n\nSince $B$ is an orthonormal basis, we have that $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]$, where ${x}_{i}=x\\cdot {q}_{i}.$ Computing the components of $x,$ we get the following: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]=\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ {x}_{2} & =[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}\\end{aligned}]=1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have \n\n$$\n[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}].\n$$" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357650 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357651 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357652 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357653 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1000 #edb/ref 17592186357654 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1041 "selection" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1104 #edb/ref 17592186357654 13194139535616 true] [17592186357649 1110 #uuid "0f157ac8-0538-5e2f-a79d-a1816e8f4298" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357650 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357650 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535616 true] [17592186357650 1111 #uuid "b354047d-d921-5251-8048-7155b847509f" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357651 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357651 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535616 true] [17592186357651 1111 #uuid "32a825ef-d817-5dfa-b570-539f7289bfe7" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357652 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357652 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535616 true] [17592186357652 1111 #uuid "aaa97402-e5a7-5f24-9fa6-6a10b5d24d79" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357653 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}+1 \\\\ 1-\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357653 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535616 true] [17592186357653 1111 #uuid "3577c778-45c1-5e5f-9c2a-59a38870e981" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357654 1034 "[\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{3}-1 \\\\ 1+\\sqrt{3}\\end{aligned}]" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357654 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139535616 true] [17592186357654 1111 #uuid "59780a65-0686-5308-ae83-3a9c09a2682d" 13194139535616 true] [17592186357655 1017 #edb/ref 175921